                <pb facs="0217" n="111" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg111"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Egan to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-04-24"><hi rendition="#italic">April 24,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Egan asks whether he can act with Brazilian minister and French chargé
                    d’affaires in an endeavor to restore peace, the indication being that mediation
                    would be accepted by the Government and the opposition.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
